langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle$, and $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\, \\mid = \\sqrt{19}$. Find $x$." 13194139534688 false] [17592186059470 1100 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" 13194139534688 true] [17592186059470 1145 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$" 13194139534688 true] [17592186059470 1145 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 2 x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 2 x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - x \\mathbf{i} - 3 x \\mathbf{j} + 3 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - x , - 3 x , 3 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}| \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | & = \\sqrt{( - x {)}^{2} + ( - 3 x {)}^{2} + {3}^{2}} \\\\  & = \\sqrt{10 {x}^{2} + 9} .\\end{array}$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl} & | \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | = \\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10 {x}^{2} + 9} = \\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10 {x}^{2} + 9 = 19 \\\\  & 10 {x}^{2} = 10 \\\\  & {x}^{2} = 1\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1$." 13194139534688 false] [17592186059661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303453 13194139534688 true] [17592186059661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303460 13194139534688 true] [17592186059661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303467 13194139534688 true] [17592186059661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303474 13194139534688 true] [17592186059661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303482 13194139534688 true] [17592186059662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303439 13194139534688 true] [17592186059662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303446 13194139534688 true] [17592186059662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303489 13194139534688 true] [17592186059662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303494 13194139534688 true] [17592186059662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303499 13194139534688 true] [17592186303439 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303440 13194139534688 true] [17592186303439 1089 "q-103540" 13194139534688 true] [17592186303439 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534688 true] [17592186303439 1100 "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" 13194139534688 true] [17592186303439 1113 #uuid "f571d284-38ad-50ae-b89e-87bf4db6e4ab" 13194139534688 true] [17592186303439 1145 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & 